  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Gu Ye brings Fang Yuan from Old Earth City by green crystal hero’s path, landing on a southeast plaza over a hundred thousand li away. Street lamps every few hundred steps cast only weak yellow light for dozens of steps, so long stretches stay dim and the upper paths feel abandoned while faint noise rises from below.",
      "chapters": [
        739
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_gu_ye",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "loc_old_earth_city"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The giant city is pitch black, resembling a giant beast sprawled on the ground. Every tile and brick emits a dense darkness that dyes the surroundings black, denser toward the center. Street lamps every few hundred steps cast only weak dusky yellow light for dozens of steps, leaving long stretches of darkness between them. It is almost as large as a mountain and is divided into seven floors.",
      "chapters": [
        739
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gu Ye divides the city into seven floors: the lower five for mortal Gu Masters, one above for immortal zombies and related people, and the highest for the conference hall where three rank seven immortal zombies are stationed year round.",
      "chapters": [
        739
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "floors-and-hall",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The discussion hall door was made by the founder of Northern Plains Zombie Alliance; only Northern Plains immortal zombies can push it open, and the city has expanded many times while keeping that door on purpose.",
      "chapters": [
        741
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "floors-and-hall",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_northern_plains",
        "fac_zombie_alliance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Northern Plains Zombie Alliance’s main headquarters sits above the entrance of Earth Trench and commits much of the alliance’s strength to guarding it. Below the city a giant gully opens in the dense darkness as that entrance; Yin Liu Gong, Dragon Commander Ye Cha, and Huang Quan Weng take turns watching it. Earth Trench is far larger and deeper than the city, and the alliance has not explored its true depths.",
      "chapters": [
        743
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "guarded-entrance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_earth_earth_trench",
        "char_yin_liu_gong",
        "char_dragon_commander_ye_cha",
        "char_huang_quan_weng"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Sixth Hair tells Fang Yuan that every Zombie Alliance branch is being targeted, and that the city would already have been ransacked if it had not sunk into Earth Trench. He adds that the super Gu formation sits inside the city, so getting the Immortal Gu out of it will take him time.",
      "chapters": [
        1077
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "sinking-into-earth-trench",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_sixth_hair",
        "sys_super_gu_formation",
        "sys_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Later narration states the headquarters had sunken into Earth Trench, where only Shadow Sect’s remaining members could find it.",
      "chapters": [
        1164
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "sinking-into-earth-trench",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_shadow_sect"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Northern Plains Zombie Alliance’s Immortal Gu are all still hidden inside the city. The city lies hidden deep inside Earth Trench.",
      "chapters": [
        1256
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "immortal-gu-cache",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
